{"id":"n-20261009-s43zcv","category":"tech","display_title":"Iron Fist Protects US Bradleys","display_title_he":"חץ דורבן מגן על הברדלי האמריקאי","short_summary":"The US Army has started integrating Elbit's Iron Fist active protection system into upgraded Bradley fighting vehicles. This deployment highlights a major defense collaboration between the United States and Israeli defense industries.","english_level":"C1","words":462,"reading_time":3,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/B020311f_-_SPC_Gruda_responds_to_call_while_manning_M240B.png/960px-B020311f_-_SPC_Gruda_responds_to_call_while_manning_M240B.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"SPC Bill Putnam, 131st MPAD, U.S. Army · Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B020311f_-_SPC_Gruda_responds_to_call_while_manning_M240B.png"},"sources":[{"name":"Walla","domain":"finance.walla.co.il","url":"https://finance.walla.co.il/item/3871494","title":"מערכת חץ דורבן הישראלית מתחילה להגן על לוחמי החי\"ר של ארה\"ב","published_at":"2026-10-09T08:07:00.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-09T08:07:00.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-09T06:28:18.990Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["The United States Army has officially begun the operational deployment of its first Bradley fighting vehicles outfitted with the Israeli Iron Fist active protection system, developed by Elbit Systems. According to official reports, this initiative represents a significant milestone in modernizing the ground forces to counter diverse contemporary battlefield threats, ranging from advanced anti-tank guided missiles and rocket-propelled grenades to suicide drones and loitering munitions. For the Israeli defense sector, this milestone underscores a profound vote of confidence from the world's leading military force in domestic defense technology.","Rather than manufacturing entirely new chassis, the program relies on comprehensive structural and mechanical overhauls of existing vehicles to meet the M2A4 and M2A4E1 standards. While the upgrades include new engines, transmissions, and suspension components, the most critical modifications involve the electrical infrastructure. Legacy Bradley platforms lacked the immense electrical power required to operate advanced radars, electronic components, and high-powered interceptors. Consequently, this deep modernization transforms vintage combat vehicles into highly survivable, digitally integrated platforms.","General Dynamics Ordnance and Tactical Systems acts as the prime contractor interfacing directly with the Pentagon. Initial procurement contracts have surpassed two hundred million dollars to equip a complete armored brigade combat team, with future expansion options potentially raising the total value by hundreds of millions of dollars. Deliveries and tactical integration will continue progressively over the upcoming years through combined exercises and training programs.","Adopting Iron Fist for the Bradley highlights distinct technological divergences from Rafael's established Trophy active protection system. While Trophy utilizes a dense cloud of metal pellets to physically shatter incoming warheads at a safe distance, Iron Fist deploys a compact, consumable interceptor that explodes adjacent to incoming threats, neutralizing them primarily via a concentrated blast wave. This methodology significantly minimizes secondary shrapnel hazards, making it notably safer for dismounted infantry troops operating in close proximity to armored vehicles. Furthermore, the system's lighter weight and compact footprint make it exceptionally suitable for medium and light combat vehicles that cannot support the heavier load of the Trophy architecture.","Meanwhile, the US military maintains its reliance on Rafael's Trophy system for its M1A2 Abrams main battle tank fleet. However, responding to operational lessons from the conflict in Ukraine regarding the excessive weight and cumbersomeness of current heavy tanks, the Pentagon canceled the SEPv4 upgrade initiative to prioritize the completely new M1E3 tank development program. In this future vehicle design, active protection mechanisms will be fully integrated into the internal framework rather than added as external modules, with Rafael and Leonardo DRS already advancing lightweight modular versions. Similarly, the Israel Defense Forces distributes its defensive systems across different platforms, utilizing Trophy on Merkava Mark 4 tanks and Namer heavy personnel carriers, while lighter wheeled Eitan armored vehicles and upcoming D9 bulldozers receive Iron Fist."],"facts":[{"fact":"The United States Army has officially begun receiving the first Bradley fighting vehicles equipped with Elbit's Iron Fist active protection system.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The initial contracts exceed 200 million dollars for an entire armored brigade combat team, with a potential for hundreds of millions more.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"General Dynamics Ordnance and Tactical Systems serves as the prime contractor working with the Pentagon.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Bradley vehicles are existing platforms thoroughly upgraded to the M2A4E1 standard, featuring completely overhauled electrical infrastructures to support radars and interceptors.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Iron Fist uses a small consumable interceptor that detonates near the threat to neutralize it with a powerful blast wave, reducing secondary fragmentation compared to Rafael's Trophy system.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The US Army continues to rely on Rafael's Trophy system for its M1A2 Abrams main battle tanks.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"United States Army","lemma":"United States Army","pos":"noun","he":"צבא ארצות הברית","name":"true"},{"text":"officially","lemma":"officially","pos":"adverb","he":"באופן רשמי","name":false},{"text":"begun","